WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.002
-Yes! That is what
I'm talking about.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.871
Looking good, bud.
Looking good.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.739
-We can't forget.
We can't forget.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.842
Everybody's to get out there
and do their thing.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:12.144
-You actually been talking a lot
about the importance of voting

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:14.247
and encouraging people to vote.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.882
And, you know, I follow you
on all the socials.

00:00:16.882 --> 00:00:18.918
You found a different way

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.787
to bring attention to this
by posting this photo.

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.957
Come on. Come on.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:27.460
-Yeah. Listen.
-Come on.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.728
-I got to tell you, I don't know
what's going on there.

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:32.632
I had good lighting.
I had good lighting.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.733
-Oh, please.
-I had -- Listen, Jimmy.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.101
I had just moisturized.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.337
The cocoa butter
was in full effect.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.205
You know what I'm saying?
-There's a couple abs in there.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:43.175
I will never see --
I think I almost have one ab.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:44.543
I found it the other way.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:46.412
It was, like, floating around --
It's that or a hernia.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:49.449
But it's something, and I go,
"Ooh, this is something."

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:52.085
I could never post
something like that,

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:55.021
but you got to get people out
and get people talking.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.123
-You got to do
what you got to do, man.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.160
Listen. If showing a little bit
of flesh means that people

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.895
will be incentivized
to go ahead and register,

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.263
it's an important vote.

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:06.565
I'll press a little flesh.
Why not?

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:08.467
-You've always been
in good shape.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:11.270
And I was seeing the things
you've been doing in quarantine.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.907
Have you taught yourself
anything or any hobbies?

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.742
-Okay. So, check it out.

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:20.312
I did start taking piano lessons
during the quarantine.

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:21.781
-You did?
-Now, listen, I cant --

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.183
I can't get out there
with you and The Roots

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:25.651
or anything like that,

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:27.586
but I can play a few little
jingles around the house.

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:29.288
And it's relaxing.
-Wow.

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:30.890
-It relaxes me.
-That's amazing.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.092
-I have an instructor,
who's a really cool guy.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:35.562
He's about ten years
younger than me.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:39.098
And I have a ping-pong table
in my garage.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:41.367
Now, I don't get a chance to
play ping-pong with anybody,

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.569
but he saw the table
and he's like, "Do you play?"

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:44.737
And I was like, "You know.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.839
I do a little something.
Like, I'm all right."

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:49.609
He's like, "Do you maybe --
You want to play with me?

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.244
And I'm like, "Yeah, bud.
Yeah, I'll play with you."

00:01:52.244 --> 00:01:53.780
So we were like two kids.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.981
After like 30 minutes
on the piano,

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:58.851
he's like, "Okay, so...
you want to go play now?"

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:00.586
And I was like, "Yeah."

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.488
And my wife is like,
"What are you guys doing?"

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.357
I was like, "Oh, we're going to
go play a little ping-pong.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.658
We good?"

00:02:06.658 --> 00:02:09.762
Every piano lesson, Jimmy,
is 30 minutes on the piano

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:14.233
and about 2 to 2 1/2 hours
on the ping-pong table.

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.135
-You have a new friend.
You're like a little kid.

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.537
-I have a new --

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.139
It's the best thing because
you're socially distanced.

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:23.408
It's one of those things where
you play hard, you're sweating.

00:02:23.408 --> 00:02:24.744
Like, you're sweating.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.312
You're not thinking about
anything else.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.448
And I think more than anything,
there is so much

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.250
on people's minds
during this pandemic.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.018
It was nice to have something
to turn it off for a second

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:35.988
and just try to hit
this little ball over the net.

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:39.958
-I saw, also, that your youngest
son, I believe, he's 5?

00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:44.063
-Amaré. Yeah, he's 5.
-He tried to cut his own hair.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.132
I thought that was pretty funny.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:49.302
How did that go?
And when did you find out?

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:54.540
-My little Negro,
African-American, Black child,

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:58.745
God bless him, he saw some
scissors just in the house.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.713
And his hair was growing longer,
and he's like,

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.715
"I'm gonna help everybody else
in the house out.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:05.985
Like, I can see that there's
a need that needs to be met."

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.920
So he goes,
he picks up the scissors,

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.322
and he got himself, like,
right in the middle.

00:03:10.322 --> 00:03:12.191
And my wife
took a picture of him.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:13.826
And God bless him.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.728
It's not like he thought
he was in trouble or anything.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:17.396
I was like, "Amaré,
did you just cut your hair?"

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:21.067
And he's like, "Yeah.
It needed to be cut, so I did."

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.603
And I was like, "All right.
Well, look in the mirror, bro.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.573
Like, how do you feel about it?
Are you enjoying it?"

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:29.108
And he's like,
"Yeah, this is great."

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.477
-It's, like, parted
in the middle.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.579
-I love that --
Listen. I have two little boys.

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.481
On the TV show,
I have three little girls.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.550
But with the little boy, I just
take out the razor, man.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.620
I take that ish
all the way down,

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.754
and then we just
start over again.

00:03:42.754 --> 00:03:44.957
-And he was cool with it?

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.692
-He was totally cool.
He loved it.

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:48.894
-Sterling, I want to talk about
"This is Us" because --

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:51.230
Man, I'm so psyched
that you guys are back.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.232
I'm happy
you are doing it safely.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:54.701
But how did it feel to be back?

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.736
Is it different? Is it odd?

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:59.338
-It's different,
and it feels like home.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:00.940
You're away from it,
and you're like,

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.875
"I want to get back
to this thing that I love."

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.443
-Yep.
-Like, I love it so much.

00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:06.445
Not only the stories,
but the people.

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:08.013
You know what I'm saying?
-Yeah.

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:10.583
-So however you can get back
to each other safely,

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.452
it feels so good, man.
Like, honest to goodness.

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:15.421
There's a ton of protocols
in place

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.523
to make sure
that we can do it safely,

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:20.660
but we're all overjoyed
to be back on the air.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.663
-I read somewhere that
the creator, the writer.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:27.065
Is it -- Dan Fogelman.
That he wanted this to come out

00:04:27.065 --> 00:04:32.338
now, as soon as it can,
because you somehow incorporated

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:35.974
the pandemic
and also Black Lives Matter

00:04:35.974 --> 00:04:38.744
movement into the show.
-Yeah.

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:41.413
-That's going to be interesting
to see how you guys do that.

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:44.684
-I think Dan, being sort of the
civic-minded individual,

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.819
felt like we had created
something

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:49.121
that would connect
with the populace.

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:52.525
I think the special thing
about our show is that everyone

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:55.428
gets a chance to see a
reflection of themselves in it.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.630
I think
leading up to this election,

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.899
I think he felt like
it was important

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.133
that people sees themselves.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.568
-Everyone's looking forward
to it.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.303
I'll definitely be watching.
I want to show everyone a clip

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:05.804
from the season premiere.

00:05:05.804 --> 00:05:08.908
Here is Sterling K. Brown in the
new season of "This is Us."

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.609
Take a look.

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:13.445
-Daphne says if you touch your
face, you automatically get it.

00:05:13.445 --> 00:05:15.514
-You might.
-Deja, come on.

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:19.285
-Hey, this thing is serious.
People need to wake the hell up.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.387
-Okay. Yeah. Understood.

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.389
But, Mom, if you guys
change your mind

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.791
and want to come stay here...

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:28.227
Okay. I know.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.295
-Holy crap.

00:05:30.295 --> 00:05:32.064
-Hey, Mom, I'll call you later.

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:33.966
I love you.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.802
Well, the clinical trial
is officially postponed.

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:38.804
After all that.

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:40.239
Thank God Mom and Miguel

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.640
went to the cabin
before St. Louis.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.411
She said she's comfortable.
She'll ride it out there.

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.613
-Tom Hanks got it.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.916
-Hanks got the corona?
-Hanks got the corona.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:54.086
-Oh. I gotta call Kate.
-Randall --

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:57.523
-No, it's Tom Hanks, babe.
She got to hear this from me.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:59.625
♪♪

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.794
-People are going to
wake up now.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:04.763
-Sterling K. Brown, thank you
so much for being here.

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:06.566
You know it means a lot to me
that you come on the show.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:08.267
-Always.
-"This is Us" returns for

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.070
a two-hour season premiere
tomorrow night

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.539
at 9:00 p.m. on NBC.

